    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0169" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.1/15½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Counselor for the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lansing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: Surely if Mr. Morgan’s
                    information is correct as stated in the enclosed letter,<anchor n="1a"
                        xml:id="d91-f1"/> the British Government is in danger of taking a very
                    unjustifiable and high-handed action. I would very much like your carefully
                    considered opinion on the subject.</p>
                <p>Cordially yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d91-f1" n="1a" xml:id="d91-f1-content">
